(The problem as given is unsolvable because the goal requires the single `route_task_profile_alpha` to be linked (via `candidate_task_profile_linked`) to four different candidates (`origin_availability_alpha`, `destination_availability_alpha`, `shift_candidate_alpha`, and `shift_candidate_beta`). The domain’s `attach_task_profile` action can only link a route‑task‑profile to one candidate at a time (its `route_task_profile_available` precondition becomes false after the first link, preventing additional links). Since there is no way to have `route_task_profile_alpha` simultaneously linked to all four candidates, none of the required goal predicates can be satisfied, making a valid plan impossible under the given domain and initial state.)
